#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0163 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "dataset ADLBC structure=BDS. Columns STUDYID(Char), USUBJID(Char), PARAMCD(Char), BTOXGR(Char). ZERO data rows (the metadata separator `---` immediately followed by the closing `---`). The firing shape is DECLARED: BTOXGR is a column, ATOXGR is not. Presence is a property of the declared schema, not of the rows, so BroadcastFold decides the dataset-constant Check against the original context before the 0-row synthetic zero-column table is ever built, and datasetBroadcastResult emits exactly ONE violation at internal row 0 = reported row 1. Pin `row=1` and NO value pin - extractOutputValues yields an empty string past the end of a 0-row table. Precedent pmda/PMDA-AD0170/PMDA-AD0170-invalid_empty_dataset-ADTTE.cdt."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col BTOXGR type=Char
---
---
